+# Aegis Production Enhancements: KMS, Observability, Edge Resilience, Gatekeeper Audit
+
+This patch (aegis-production-enhancements-2026-02-13.patch) provides:
+- Vault Helm installer script to deploy HA Vault and bootstrap operator steps (tools/install_vault_helm.sh)
+- Production receipt signer using Vault Transit (services/signing/receipt_signer_vault.py)
+- Production encrypt-store using Vault Transit + object storage (services/storage/encrypt_store_vault.py)
+- Consent check + enhanced retrieval guard previously added — these integrate with the above
+- Gatekeeper audit collector that posts violations to MCP and/or writes CSV (tools/gatekeeper_audit_to_mcp.py)
+- Edge sync retry worker and offline drill tooling to handle network outages (services/edge/sync_retry.py, tools/edge_offline_drill.sh)
+- Observability middleware for WSGI apps (services/observability/metrics_middleware.py) and Prometheus ServiceMonitors for webhook & Triton.
+
+Deployment notes & operator tasks:
+1. Run tools/install_vault_helm.sh to install Vault (operator must initialize/unseal or configure auto-unseal with cloud KMS).
+2. Create Vault policies for transit and KV usage; create a Kubernetes auth role binding to the relevant ServiceAccounts.
+3. Ensure TRANSIT_KEY is created (vault write -f transit/keys/<name>) and that Vault token is available for CI or use Vault Agent sidecar in pods.
+4. Replace any prior stub signer/encryptor with these production services and update service env vars to point to VAULT_ADDR and TRANSIT_KEY_NAME.
+5. Deploy ServiceMonitors if you run Prometheus Operator so webhook and Triton metrics are scraped.
+6. Run tools/gatekeeper_audit_to_mcp.py periodically (cron) to post violations to MCP and track remediation.
+7. Deploy the edge sync_retry worker on edge nodes to ensure failed syncs are retried; run tools/edge_offline_drill.sh to validate fetchtoken flows.
+
+Security notes:
+- Vault should be HA and configured with secure auto-unseal, or use managed KMS-backed auto-unseal.
+- Keep VAULT_TOKEN out of repo; prefer Kubernetes auth + Vault Agent or CSI secrets provider.
+- Ensure S3 buckets and KMS policies are tight (least privilege).
+
